Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

And to be clear, these are not new bugs but rather enhanced warning detections, as far as we know. Because nimble's on-the-fly C++ compilation happens on multiple operating systems, and because we call the C++ compiler through R (R CMD SHLIB), we don't try to tune C++ compiler flags to reduce harmless warnings.  Instead they are normally suppressed from being shown in the R session unless you opt to see them.
-Perry

