Hi Ethan,

Indeed, it looks like our conjugacy checking in this case is not sophisticated enough to detect conjugacy for the `vx` parameters.

A couple thoughts:

1) I don't know that conjugate sampling here would do a lot better than a slice sampler or our default Metropolis random walk sampler. So you might try those.
2) You could write your own user-defined conjugate sampler <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-progr-with-models.html#sec:user-samplers> that you can assign to the `vx` parameters.

-chris

