Another (perhaps net easier) option would be to set up a model where nimble *does* detect this { dbeta -> stick_breaking -> dcat } conjugate relationship (this could be a simplified version of your model), then when nimble detects and assigns a conjugate sampler for the dbeta node, you could grab the conjugate sampler definition, and also inspect the structure of the inputs to it (these mostly consist of the dependent node names, IIRC), and manually add this sampler yourself to the desired model nodes (while providing the correct inputs).  This would take a little bit of "getting to know" nimble, but I think would be overall easier than writing your own conjugate sampler.

